ity in injecting drug users, according to HIV and introduction of HAART</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17085455</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ije/dyl231</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000e1;ez-Feliciano</surname><given-names>DV</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>G&#x000f3;mez</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Miranda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fern&#x000e1;ndez</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Vel&#x000e1;zquez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000ed;os-Olivares</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter-Mellado</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changes in the AIDS epidemiologic situation in Puerto Rico following health care reform and the introduction of HAART</article-title><source>Rev Panam Salud Publica</source><year>2005</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>92</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15826386</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1590/S1020-49892005000200005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>del Amo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>del Romero</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Barrasa</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>P&#x000e9;rez-Hoyos</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodr&#x000ed;guez</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>D&#x000ed;ez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Garc&#x000ed;a</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><su